%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 83557978626b43b489fb47aa61cf7b2c, type: 3}
  m_Name: LetterCatalog
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: IdleFarm.EconomyCore::LetterCatalogSO
  letters:
  - id: welcome
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: 
    newPlayersOnly: 0
    senderName: Mayor Bramble
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: Welcome to {farmName}!
    body: 'Dear {farmName},


      Welcome to the valley! This old farm has sat
      quiet for years, and we''re all so glad someone is bringing it back to life.


      I''ve
      left a sack of radish seeds in your shed. They''re quick to grow and hard to
      get wrong - just the thing for a first harvest. Choose a field, and your helpers
      will plant, water and harvest for you.


      Every harvest earns Money to
      buy more seeds, plus Coins you get to keep. Hazel at the seed stall in the
      Market has more kinds when you''re ready - here''s a little something toward
      your first packet.


      - Mayor Bramble'
    rewardKind: 1
    rewardAmount: 50
    ctaKind: 0
    ctaArg: 
  - id: compost_bay_unlock
    triggerFeatureFlag: composting_basics
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: 
    newPlayersOnly: 0
    senderName: Pippa the Tinker
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: You can build a Compost Bay!
    body: 'Hey {farmName}!


      Heard you''ve been reading up on composting. Good
      news - I can put together a Compost Bay for you now. Swing by the shop and
      grab one; your soil will thank you.


      Oh! And ask Hazel about corn. Those
      big stalks make twice the compost when a plant doesn''t make it.


      -
      Pippa'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 1
    ctaArg: 
  - id: first_run_done
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: run_ended:1
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Mayor Bramble
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: Your first harvest!
    body: 'Dear {farmName},


      What a sight - crops growing on that old farm
      again! The whole town is talking.


      Those Coins you earned are yours
      to keep. Spend them on farm upgrades and your next run will go even further.
      If you''re not sure where to start, a bigger field is never a bad idea.


      -
      Mayor Bramble'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 4
    ctaArg: 
  - id: axe_offer
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: run_ended:2
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Harry the Carpenter
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: Those trees won't chop themselves
    body: 'Howdy {farmName},


      Harry here, the carpenter down at the market.
      Noticed the woods behind your place are getting mighty overgrown. That timber''s
      yours for the taking!


      Come see me and I''ll set you up with an axe.
      Wood sells at the rack, and a good builder always needs more of it.


      -
      Harry'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 5
    ctaArg: 
  - id: first_tree
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: tree_felled
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Harry the Carpenter
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: Timber!
    body: '{farmName},


      Heard that one fall from here! Nice swing.


      Your
      wood stacks up on the rack by the woods. Sell some for Coins, but hang on to
      a pile, too. Before long you''ll want it for fuel, and I''ll have buildings
      to put up for you.


      - Harry'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 0
    ctaArg: 
  - id: pole_offer
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: run_ended:3|axe_bought
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Old Finch
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: The fish are biting
    body: 'Well now, {farmName}.


      That lake past your farm is full of perch,
      and nobody''s cast a line in it for years. Shame, that.


      Harry keeps
      a fishing pole or two in his shop. Get yourself one and come down to the water.
      Patience is the whole trick of it.


      - Old Finch'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 5
    ctaArg: 
  - id: first_fish
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: fish_caught
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Old Finch
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: Your first catch
    body: 'Ha! Knew you had it in you, {farmName}.


      Here''s something an old
      fisherman will tell you for free: watch for the whirlpools. That''s where the
      fish gather, and a line cast there gets a bite much quicker.


      - Old
      Finch'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 0
    ctaArg: 
  - id: cannery_unlock
    triggerFeatureFlag: cannery_unlocked
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: 
    newPlayersOnly: 0
    senderName: Marta
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: Jam season!
    body: 'Hello {farmName}!


      Marta here, from the jam stall. Word is you''ve
      been learning to preserve, and I couldn''t be happier!


      Have Harry build
      you a Cannery. Your crops can go into jars instead of being sold, and a good
      jar is worth far more than the fruit it came from.


      Hazel''s got strawberry
      seeds in now, too - they make the quickest jam there is!


      Save me a
      jar of strawberry?


      - Marta'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 5
    ctaArg: 
  - id: smokehouse_unlock
    triggerFeatureFlag: smokehouse_unlocked
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: 
    newPlayersOnly: 0
    senderName: Old Finch
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: A proper smokehouse
    body: '{farmName},


      So you''ve learned the old smoking ways. Good. Raw
      fish sells, but smoked fish? That''s worth several times as much.


      Harry
      can build you a Smokehouse near the lake. Keep the fire fed with wood and the
      fish will do the rest.


      - Old Finch'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 5
    ctaArg: 
  - id: cannery_built
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: built:building_cannery_built
    newPlayersOnly: 0
    senderName: Harry the Carpenter
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: Your Cannery is ready
    body: '{farmName},


      All built, and sturdy as they come! Load your Cannery
      up with crops, then keep the firebox stocked with wood.


      If the fire
      goes out, nothing spoils. The jars just wait for you.


      - Harry'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 0
    ctaArg: 
  - id: smokehouse_built
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: built:building_smokehouse_built
    newPlayersOnly: 0
    senderName: Harry the Carpenter
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: Your Smokehouse is ready
    body: '{farmName},


      Smokehouse is up! Old Finch already came by to inspect
      the chimney.


      Put raw fish in the smoker and keep the fire fed with
      wood. If it burns out, the fish just wait.


      - Harry'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 0
    ctaArg: 
  - id: first_request
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: town_request_done
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Mayor Bramble
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: The town is grateful
    body: 'Dear {farmName},


      Word gets around fast in a town this size, and
      folks are singing your praises! Every request you fill earns you Reputation.


      Fill
      the Reputation bar and you''ll earn a point to spend at your Barn, making your
      whole farm better at what it does.


      - Mayor Bramble'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 6
    ctaArg: 
  - id: first_animal
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: animal_unlocked
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Mayor Bramble
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: A new friend on the farm
    body: 'Dear {farmName},


      I hear you''ve got some company out there! Animals
      do more than keep you company - each one changes how your farm runs.


      Open
      your animals menu to put your new friend to work.


      - Mayor Bramble'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 7
    ctaArg: 
  - id: field_two
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: upgrade:zone_unlock_2
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Mayor Bramble
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: More room to grow
    body: 'Dear {farmName},


      A second field! You''re turning that old place
      into a real farm.


      Don''t forget to pick seeds for it before your next
      run - an empty field grows nothing.


      And a little secret from someone
      who''s watched plenty of farms grow: a helper can only be in one place at a
      time. If your new field is slow to get going, a second pair of hands works
      wonders. A quicker helper or a sprinkler helps too - less time hauling water
      means more time planting!


      - Mayor Bramble'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 8
    ctaArg: 
  - id: long_run_1h
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: run_survived:1h
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Mayor Bramble
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: The talk of the valley
    body: 'Dear {farmName},


      A whole hour of harvests without a break! Folks
      in town can hardly believe it.


      Please accept this small token from
      all of us. Keep it up!


      - Mayor Bramble'
    rewardKind: 2
    rewardAmount: 25
    ctaKind: 0
    ctaArg: 
  - id: long_run_3h
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: run_survived:3h
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Mayor Bramble
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: A farm to be proud of
    body: 'Dear {farmName},


      Three whole hours! Travelers are stopping in
      town just to ask about your farm.


      The council voted, and this gift
      is from all of us. Well earned.


      - Mayor Bramble'
    rewardKind: 2
    rewardAmount: 50
    ctaKind: 0
    ctaArg: 
  - id: seed_stall_intro
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: run_ended:1
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Hazel
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: Fresh seeds at my stall
    body: 'Hi {farmName}!


      Hazel here - I run the seed stall at the Market.
      Saw your radishes come up. Lovely work!


      When you''re ready to try something
      new, come see me. Carrots are next to nothing, and they sell for nearly twice
      as much.


      Once you buy a packet, that crop is yours to plant every run
      after.


      - Hazel'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 11
    ctaArg: 
  - id: regrow_bought
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: seed_bought:regrow
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Hazel
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: These ones keep giving
    body: 'Hi {farmName}!


      Good choice! That one''s a regrower. Pick it, and
      as long as the plant survives, it grows back and gives you another harvest
      - no new seed needed.


      Keep it watered and keep the pests off, and it''ll
      pay for itself many times over.


      - Hazel'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 0
    ctaArg: 
  - id: town_board_intro
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: run_ended:4
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Mayor Bramble
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: The town could use a hand
    body: 'Dear {farmName},


      Word''s getting around about your farm! A few
      of us in town could use a hand now and then, so we post what we need on the
      community board by the Market.


      Help out, and folks won''t forget it.
      Every delivery earns you Reputation, and a good name in this valley opens doors
      - your Barn will show you how.


      I''ve pinned the first request myself.


      -
      Mayor Bramble'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 10
    ctaArg: 
  - id: extra_packets
    triggerFeatureFlag: 
    triggerAnimalId: 
    triggerEvent: upgrade:zone_unlock_2
    newPlayersOnly: 1
    senderName: Hazel
    senderPortrait: {fileID: 0}
    subject: One crop, two fields?
    body: 'Hi {farmName}!


      A second field - congratulations! You can plant
      a different crop in each field, or double down on one.


      Every packet
      you own lets a crop grow in one field. Want corn in both fields to pile up
      compost, or radishes everywhere to fill a big order? Pick up a second packet
      at my stall.


      Mixing crops spreads your luck - deer and crows each have
      their favorites!


      - Hazel'
    rewardKind: 0
    rewardAmount: 0
    ctaKind: 11
    ctaArg: 
  cast:
  - id: mayor
    displayName: Mayor Bramble
    role: Mayor of the valley town, and the player's first friend.
    voice: Warm, proud, a touch formal. Speaks for the whole town and celebrates
      milestones, sometimes with a small gift. Opens "Dear {farmName}," and signs
      "- Mayor Bramble".
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - id: pippa
    displayName: Pippa the Tinker
    role: Inventor who builds gadgets for farms (Compost Bay, equipment).
    voice: Excitable and quick, loves a clever contraption. Opens "Hey {farmName}!"
      and signs "- Pippa".
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - id: harry
    displayName: Harry the Carpenter
    role: 'Runs the carpenter''s shop at the market: tools (axe, fishing pole) and
      buildings.'
    voice: Friendly, plainspoken tradesman with a folksy streak ("Howdy", "mighty").
      Practical advice about wood and building. Signs "- Harry".
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - id: finch
    displayName: Old Finch
    role: Retired fisherman who knows every inch of the lake. Also posts Town Requests.
    voice: Slow, dry, few words; fond of the lake and of patience. Opens "Well now,"
      or just the farm name. Signs "- Old Finch".
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - id: marta
    displayName: Marta
    role: Runs the jam stall; the town's preserves expert. Also posts Town Requests.
    voice: Cheerful, chatty and food-obsessed; always angling for a jar. Opens "Hello
      {farmName}!" and signs "- Marta".
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - id: pip
    displayName: Pip
    role: Kid with a picky pet rabbit. Posts Town Requests (no mail yet).
    voice: Eager and a little dramatic about the rabbit.
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - id: hazel
    displayName: Hazel
    role: Runs the seed stall at the Market. Sells every crop's seed packet.
    voice: Warm, practical, loves a bargain and a good tip about what grows well.
      Opens "Hi {farmName}!" and signs "- Hazel".
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  tips:
  - id: onboarding_mailbox
    text: Mail arrives here. Tap to read your welcome letter from the Mayor.
    when: 'First session 1/5: right after naming the farm (spotlights the mailbox)'
  - id: onboarding_field
    text: The Mayor's seeds are waiting in your shed. Tap here to choose what to
      plant.
    when: 'First session 2/5: closing the mailbox after the welcome letter (spotlights
      Field)'
  - id: onboarding_pick_seeds
    text: Tap a seed to plant it in your field, then tap Save.
    when: 'First session 3/5: seed picker open (spotlights the whole picker)'
  - id: onboarding_start_run
    text: Your helpers will plant, water and harvest for you. Tap Start Run and watch
      your farm grow!
    when: 'First session 4/5: after saving seeds (spotlights Start Run)'
  - id: onboarding_money_note
    text: 'Each harvest earns Money to buy more seeds during this run.


      Coins
      are yours to keep, even after the run ends. Spend them to grow your farm!'
    when: 'First session 5/5: the first run starts'
  - id: tip_out_of_money
    text: You're out of Money for seeds! Every harvest earns more, but seed bags
      cost more the longer a run goes. When you can't buy seeds and nothing is growing,
      the run ends.
    when: 'Any run: first time a helper can''t afford a seed bag (points at the seed
      counter)'
  - id: tip_farm_upgrades
    text: Spend your Coins here to make every run better. A bigger field is a great
      first buy!
    when: First time the Farm upgrades menu opens
  - id: tip_quests
    text: Finish daily quests to earn Gems. New quests arrive every day.
    when: First time the Quests menu opens
  - id: tip_daily_rewards
    text: Come back every day for a gift. Collect every day of the week for a bonus!
    when: First time the daily rewards calendar opens
  - id: tip_market
    text: Welcome to the market! Look around - shops here sell seeds, tools and buildings.
      Check the notice board for townsfolk who need a hand.
    when: First arrival at the Market
  - id: tip_woods_no_axe
    text: These trees are yours to chop, but you'll need an axe first. Harry the
      Carpenter sells one at the market.
    when: First arrival at the Woods without an axe
  - id: tip_woods
    text: Tap a tree to swing your axe. Each chop knocks loose some wood, and chopped
      trees grow back over time.
    when: First arrival at the Woods with an axe
  - id: tip_wood_rack
    text: Your wood piles up here. Sell it for Coins, or save it to fuel your buildings
      later.
    when: First time the Wood Rack opens
  - id: tip_lake
    text: Press and hold to aim your cast, then let go to throw. When a fish bites,
      tap or hold to reel it in. Whirlpools hold extra fish!
    when: First arrival at the Lake with a fishing pole
  - id: tip_first_catch
    text: Nice catch! Fish go to your pantry. Sell them raw, or smoke them in a Smokehouse
      for much more.
    when: First fish caught
  - id: tip_smokehouse
    text: Load raw fish into the smoker, then keep the fire burning with wood. If
      the fire goes out, nothing spoils - smoking just pauses.
    when: First time the Smokehouse opens
  - id: tip_cannery
    text: During a run, some harvested crops go into your jars instead of being sold.
      Keep the firebox full of wood and they'll become preserves worth far more.
    when: First time the Cannery opens
  - id: tip_compost
    text: Your Compost Bay turned a lost crop into compost! Spend compost to speed
      up research.
    when: First compost earned
  - id: tip_research
    text: Pick a topic to study. Research finishes over real time, even while you're
      away, and gives your farm permanent boosts.
    when: First time Research opens
  - id: tip_animals
    text: Animals change how your farm plays. Unlock them with Gems from quests and
      daily gifts, then equip one for your runs.
    when: First time the Animals menu opens
  - id: tip_town_requests
    text: Townsfolk post what they need here. Deliveries earn Reputation, and a full
      bar gives you a point to spend at your Barn. Switch to Collect during a run
      to keep harvests for requests.
    when: First time the Town Requests board opens
  - id: tip_barn
    text: Spend skill points to make your farm better at what it does. Tap a numbered
      milestone to see what it unlocks.
    when: First time the Barn (Farm Level) opens
  - id: tip_collect_sell
    text: Sell turns each harvest into Money right away, to keep your run going.
      Collect keeps harvests as items, for town requests and your jars.
    when: First run after the town-board letter (points at the Collect / Sell switch)
  - id: tip_almanac
    text: Everything you've discovered is written down here. Tap any page to see
      its numbers, including how much your upgrades have added.
    when: First time the Farmer's Almanac opens
  - id: almanac_crop_radish
    text: In and out of the ground before pests notice. Tiny payout, lightning fast.
    when: 'Almanac: Radish page'
  - id: almanac_crop_carrot
    text: Buried where crows can't reach - but deer will dig for them.
    when: 'Almanac: Carrot page'
  - id: almanac_crop_corn
    text: Tall stalks shrug off deer, and the harvest waits a while for you. Crows
      can't resist it.
    when: 'Almanac: Corn page'
  - id: almanac_crop_tomato
    text: Sturdy vines that keep on giving. Thirsty, though, and deer know where
      to find them.
    when: 'Almanac: Tomato page'
  - id: almanac_crop_strawberry
    text: Every bird in the valley knows when these are ripe. Makes the quickest
      jam at the Cannery.
    when: 'Almanac: Strawberry page'
  - id: almanac_crop_blueberry
    text: Slow to settle in, then fruits again and again. Thirsty, and a crow's favourite
      - but deer mostly leave it be.
    when: 'Almanac: Blueberry page'
  - id: almanac_crop_green_beans
    text: Quick to crop and quick to grow back. Tender, though, and deer can't get
      enough of them.
    when: 'Almanac: Green Beans page'
  - id: almanac_crop_green_pepper
    text: Tough and long-lived. Crows ignore the green fruit, but deer nibble the
      leaves - plant it where crows are the problem.
    when: 'Almanac: Green Pepper page'
  - id: almanac_crop_red_pepper
    text: The green pepper's twin, left to ripen. Too hot for deer, but crows can't
      resist the red - plant it where deer are the problem.
    when: 'Almanac: Red Pepper page'
  - id: almanac_pest_deer
    text: Deer wander in from the woods and graze on your fields. They go easy on
      seeds but hit young plants hardest. Fences keep them out, and a dog will chase
      them off.
    when: 'Almanac: Deer page'
  - id: almanac_pest_crow
    text: Crows swoop down and peck at your crops - fresh seeds and ripe berries
      most of all. A scarecrow scares them off.
    when: 'Almanac: Crows page'
  - id: tip_seed_stall
    text: Buy a seed packet once and that crop is yours to plant every run. The mystery
      packets are still waiting to be discovered!
    when: First time Hazel's seed stall opens
  - id: tip_regrow
    text: This crop regrows! As long as the plant survives after it's picked, it
      grows more - no new seed needed.
    when: First regrowing crop harvested in a run
  - id: tip_barn_spend
    text: You have a point to spend! Tap + to level up a skill. Each level makes
      your farm a little better at that job.
    when: Barn opened with a skill point to spend (points at a + button)
  - id: tip_extra_packet
    text: Each packet lets a crop grow in one field. Buy another to plant it in more
      fields at once - great for going all-in on compost, jam or a big town order.
    when: Hazel's stall opened once a crop can take a 2nd packet (more fields than
      packets)
  - id: tip_idle_field
    text: This field is still waiting its turn - your helper has its hands full with
      your other crops! Another helper, a speedier one, or a sprinkler would lend
      a hand.
    when: A run where a field with a crop chosen is still bare after a few minutes
